cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Smallest witnesses by girth for rad(n) | f(n)"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Ellena Godoy"
    given-names: "Jorge"
abstract: >-
  For a multiplicative function f, let S(f) be the set of integers n with
  rad(n) dividing f(n), and let the covering digraph of n have the primes
  dividing n as vertices with an edge q -> p whenever p divides f(q^e), where
  q^e is the exact power of q in n. This work computes the smallest member of
  S(f) of each girth, for f = sigma, sigma* and phi*. Two theorems: any minimal
  witness of girth k has exactly k distinct prime factors and a covering
  digraph that is a pure directed cycle; and its largest prime is bounded by
  roughly the square root of any known witness divided by the primorial of
  k-2. The second bound makes the enumeration finite, so all eighteen published
  values are proved minimal rather than minimal among the primes examined. Four
  of them had not been computed before, the largest near 3.2e16. All results
  are verified by independent implementations and cross-checked against the
  count of prime-abundant numbers published by Pollack and Pomerance (2012).
keywords:
  - number theory
  - arithmetic functions
  - sum of divisors
  - prime-abundant numbers
  - covering digraph
  - girth
  - integer sequences
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 2.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-03"
references:
